From: Hazel Smith <hazel@hazelesque.uk>
Subject: build.sbt: bump V.protobuf 3.15.6 -> 4.32.0 to match system protoc

protoc 5.32 (cports' `protobuf-protoc`) generates Java code that
references com.google.protobuf.RuntimeVersion,
com.google.protobuf.Generated, GeneratedMessage.isStringEmpty,
LazyStringArrayList.emptyList, etc.  None of those exist in
protobuf-java 3.15.6 — they were added in the 4.27 series along
with the protobuf-java major-version reset to 4.x.

Bump the runtime to 4.32.0 to match protoc 5.32's codegen.  The
protobuf-java APIs scip-java actually uses (parseFrom, builders,
iterators, *OrBuilder interfaces) are stable across the bump;
the changes are additive and concentrated in the generated-code
helper classes.

This is the minimum bump needed — picking 4.32.0 specifically
to match cports' `protobuf-protoc` 5.32.x.

diff --git a/build.sbt b/build.sbt
--- a/build.sbt
+++ b/build.sbt
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@

 lazy val V =
   new {
-    val protobuf = "3.15.6"
+    val protobuf = "4.32.0"
     val protoc =
       "3.17.3" // the oldest protoc version with Apple M1 support, see https://github.com/scalapb/ScalaPB/issues/1024#issuecomment-860126568
     val coursier = "2.1.9"
